<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank says not selling gold.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank says not selling gold.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Thursday it had not been selling its reserves of gold reserves in recent weeks.</p>
<p>Increasing rumours of European central bank sales have rocked the gold market this week, pushing bullion to its lowest price in more than three years.</p>
<p>But Bert Groothof, a spokesman for the Nederlandsche Bank, said the Dutch central bank was not behind the sales.</p>
<p>&quot;We didn't do anything with our gold,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
